# Ambrose Fennimore, travel writer (NPC plan batch 2; docs/plans/npc_depth_and_quests.md): eleven years in the valley and
# nine hundred pages into a guidebook that rates everything in stars. He stands by the signpost at the Old Svalich
# crossroads by day. Chapter one is a side quest, Fennimore's Guide: The Tser Pool: he isn't sure the camp's famous
# plum stew is plum; Old Dorina, at the pot, tells the truth (tasting it is enough; asking gently shortcuts it). No
# fight, nothing locked behind a roll. His other chapters come with the later regions. Lines drafted by Gemini through
# the ai-bridge, edited; every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ start
if quest.fennimores_guide == done
Fennimore [weary]: Ah, it is you. I am currently grading the afternoon weather: one star. Damp, grey, and entirely derivative of yesterday.
Fennimore: You have not heard from anyone up the road whether it intends to improve before winter, have you?
-> menu
endif
if flag.fennimore_met
Fennimore [smile]: Most obliged for the company. I am here by the signpost, or on the road, or wherever the road chooses to leave me.
-> menu
endif
set fennimore_met
Narrator: A neat man in a good coat gone shabby at the cuffs stands by the signpost, pencil in hand and satchel at his hip.
Narrator: He squints at the rotten wood, makes a small mark in a thick ledger, and looks up as you approach.
Fennimore [smile]: Good day. Make a note, if you keep notes: the crossroads signpost is one star. Legible, if you already know where you are.
Fennimore: Ambrose Fennimore, at your service. Eleven years in this valley, and nine hundred pages into its only reliable guidebook.
Fennimore: It is a work of great patience. Every inn, every bridge, every moderately polite ghost, all graded on a five-star scale.
Fennimore: Tell me, have you by any chance come up from the Vistani camp at Tser Pool?
-> menu

~ menu
* [if not quest.fennimores_guide] May we see the book? -> book
* [if quest.fennimores_guide == known] We found out what is in the stew. -> report
* [ends:fennimores_guide] [if quest.fennimores_guide == asked and (flag.tser_pool_brawl_won or flag.vistani_turned_hostile)] The Tser Pool camp has turned on us; we cannot get near Old Dorina's pot. -> scrap
* [ends:radus_unsellable_horse if flag.dinte_led and (flag.tser_pool_brawl_won or flag.vistani_turned_hostile)] [if quest.radus_unsellable_horse == offered] There is a horse for sale at the Tser Pool camp. -> svalich_road/radus_horse:fennimore_horse
* [ends:radus_unsellable_horse] [if quest.radus_unsellable_horse == buyer_found and (flag.tser_pool_brawl_won or flag.vistani_turned_hostile)] Radu's camp has turned on us, so there is no one left to pay his fifteen gold. -> svalich_road/radus_horse:camp_unpaid
* [if quest.dumitrus_visitor == asked] A boy at Krezk's gate would like a visitor. -> krezk/dumitrus_visitor:fennimore_ask
* [if not flag.eggs_fennimore_pocket] What's moving in your coat? -> pocket
* [if quest.fennimores_guide and not flag.eggs_rival_guide_given] Have you any rivals in the guidebook trade? -> rival
* Goodbye. -> END

~ book
Fennimore: Look here. I keep the proofs in order of the road, so a traveller may read as he walks.
Fennimore: "The Crossroads Signpost: one star. Points faithfully toward two places you should not go."
Fennimore: "The Crossroads Gallows: one star. Serviceable timber, poor view, no seating."
Fennimore: "The Blue Water Inn, Vallaki: two stars. Wolves." And beneath that, "Tser Pool Camp: three stars. The plum stew is excellent."
Fennimore [weary]: Only I have underlined "plum" twice in pencil. My tongue says onion, hare, woodsmoke, and something considerably older than a fruit.
* [if not flag.tser_pool_brawl_won and not flag.vistani_turned_hostile] Can we find out about the stew? -> ask
* Another time. -> menu

~ ask
Fennimore: A guidebook that guesses at its soups is no better than a rumor, and this valley has rumors enough.
Fennimore: I would go back and ask Old Dorina myself, but she looks at my notebook the way a butcher looks at a stray dog.
Fennimore: If your road takes you past her fire, find out what is truly at the bottom of that iron pot.
Fennimore: I will pay ten gold pieces for the verified recipe. An unconfirmed fact is a blemish on the page.
Fennimore: Do mind your manners by the wagons, though: Stanimir's people have a brisk way with guests who forget themselves.
Fennimore [weary]: If the camp closes its curtains to you, I cannot pay a copper for a recipe no living soul can confirm.
quest fennimores_guide asked
Fennimore [smile]: Most obliged. You will find me here by the signpost, or on the road, or wherever the road chooses to leave me.
-> END

# --- Old Dorina at the Tser Pool stewpot (tser_camp:dorina's menu jumps here) ---

~ dorina_ask
Old Dorina: What is in it? Plums, child. Good dark plums, four big onions, and a fat hare Radu caught by the water.
Old Dorina: A pinch of salt, a heel of black bread to thicken the liquor, and whatever herbs were not drowned by the rain.
Old Dorina [weary]: That is all that went in today. What was already waiting for it in the iron is another matter.
* (Taste the stew.) -> dorina_taste
* [Persuasion DC 12] (Ask her, gently, about the bottom of the pot.) -> dorina_truth | dorina_shy
* Never mind. -> svalich_road/tser_camp:dorina

~ dorina_taste
Narrator: You lift a spoonful from the dark broth. It is sweet with plum at first, then smoky, rich with onion and game.
Narrator: Underneath all three sits a deeper, heavier taste, dark as cellar stone and older than anything grown this year.
Narrator: Old Dorina watches your throat as you swallow, her hands resting flat on the handle of her ladle.
-> dorina_truth

~ dorina_truth
quest fennimores_guide known
Old Dorina: Sixty years that pot has hung over my fire, and for sixty years no one has seen the iron at the bottom.
Old Dorina: Every night we eat it down to the last three fingers, and every morning I build the new stew on top of the old.
Old Dorina: The stock at the very bottom is older than Stanimir. It remembers winters his mother forgot.
Old Dorina [sad]: The night my husband walked out toward the road and was carried home, my silver wedding spoon slipped from my hand into the boil.
Old Dorina [sad]: I never fished it out. You do not empty a pot that keeps the camp alive just to go looking for silver.
Old Dorina [smile]: So it stays down there, seasoning the broth. Nobody who eats from my ladle leaves with a thin belly.
-> END

~ dorina_shy
Old Dorina [angry]: Enough questions! What are you, clerks for the devil up the hill, counting every onion in an old woman's pot?
Old Dorina: Sit down, finish your bowl while it has heat in it, and keep your noses out of my iron.
-> dorina_ask

# --- Back at the signpost ---

~ report
quest fennimores_guide done
gold +10
Fennimore [smile]: Sixty years! Never emptied once, and a silver wedding spoon resting at the bottom like a river stone.
Fennimore: Oh, that is first-rate. That is the sort of detail a man stays eleven years in the fog to record.
Fennimore: Let me rub out that shameful little question mark and write it properly while the lead is sharp.
Fennimore: "Tser Pool: three stars. The stew is plum, onion, hare and sixty years. Ask for the bottom."
Fennimore [smile]: Read that aloud and tell me it does not make you hungry and slightly reflective at the same time.
Fennimore: Here are your ten gold pieces, well earned and duly noted under research expenses.
Fennimore: I shall stay by this post and start the next chapter. If you find any of my facts wanting along the road, do tell me before I go to press.
-> END

# --- The camp turned on the party before Dorina was asked (sq-stuck, finding 127): the quest is lost, not stuck ---

~ scrap
quest fennimores_guide unverified
Fennimore [weary]: Ah. That is a bereavement for the culinary appendix, though I am glad to see you still have all your fingers.
Fennimore: I must leave the entry as "plum?" with a query in the margin, which sits on a clean page like a grease spot.
Fennimore: You will understand that I cannot pay ten gold pieces for a question mark; I can supply those myself for nothing.
Fennimore: Let me strike a star from the Tser Pool entry and write "presently closed to inquiries" beneath it.
Fennimore [sad]: It is a pity, all the same: a sixty-year broth deserves better than a guess from the road.
-> menu

# --- Two winks (easter-egg plan R2, docs/story/eggs.md): his research assistant, and his rival ----------------------
# Drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge and edited (docs/plans/gemini_eggs/r2/); unvoiced.

~ pocket
set eggs_fennimore_pocket
Fennimore [smile]: My research assistant, who has lived in my left breast pocket since the fog closed behind me. Or possibly since the Tuesday after.
Fennimore: He samples the tavern bread before I risk my teeth. If he refuses a crust, I deduct two stars on principle.
* [if spell:speak_with_animals] Ask the assistant what he makes of the valley. -> pocket_speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_animals] [knows:speak_with_animals] (Cast Speak with Animals, and ask the assistant what he makes of the valley.) -> pocket_cast
* (Leave the assistant to his work.) -> menu

~ pocket_cast
cast speak_with_animals
if check.last
-> pocket_speaks
endif
-> menu

# Speak with Animals (2024 PHB): a hamster with a very high opinion of itself.
~ pocket_speaks
Narrator: The scrap of fur plants both paws on the pocket seam and bares two yellow teeth. "In my true den above the sky-roof I am taller than the tall-trees, and the wolves run under my belly like beetles. This smallness is a brief inconvenience."
Narrator: "Meanwhile, tell your pack: the wet shiny parts in the face. Those first. Always those first."
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Easy. Pocket-sized terror wants us to start with the peepers. I'll allow it.
-> menu

~ rival
set eggs_rival_guide_given
Fennimore [angry]: There is one. A charlatan with one glass eye and no shame whatsoever, whose monster book outsells mine ten to one on the strength of pure invention.
Fennimore [weary]: He has never stood in the same county as half the beasts he describes. On page forty-two he claims the owlbear is affectionate if scratched behind the beak.
Fennimore [sad]: Take my copy, please, before I wear the margins through with pencil.
give rival_monster_guide
-> menu

